# Restored 2026-09-21 from the Arch backup (@home-2026-09-18). Vivaldi writes these
# files itself when a PWA is installed and never again, so a profile that is copied
# onto a new machine keeps its web apps and loses its launchers. The profile here is
# intact -- `vivaldi-stable --app-id=<id>` opens the app -- so only this file was
# missing from fuzzel.
#
# ONE EDIT against the backup copy: Exec was `/opt/vivaldi/vivaldi`, which is the Arch
# package layout and does not exist under NixOS. `vivaldi-stable` is the name the flake
# provides (hosts/desktop/default.nix wraps nixpkgs' `vivaldi`, which installs its
# binary as `vivaldi`), and is the same name the sway config already uses.
#
# 2026-09-23: pinned to the work account. Two Google accounts share the Default profile
# and the bare start URL opens whichever one Google currently calls account 0 -- the
# personal one, lately. `--app-launch-url-for-shortcuts-menu-item` is the flag Vivaldi
# itself uses for manifest shortcuts (see the YouTube entry); it opens the app window at
# an in-scope URL instead of start_url. `?authuser=<email>` rather than `/u/1/`: the
# numeric slot is the sign-in order and flips -- History has mail/u/0 resolving to both
# accounts. The personal account is the `-Default-shad.desktop` sibling.
[Desktop Entry]
Version=1.0
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Name=Google Chat Bruce
Exec=vivaldi-stable --profile-directory=Default --app-id=pommaclcbfghclhalboakcipcmmndhcj --app-launch-url-for-shortcuts-menu-item=https://chat.google.com/?authuser=younes.el-alami@bruce.work
Icon=vivaldi-pommaclcbfghclhalboakcipcmmndhcj-Default
StartupWMClass=crx_pommaclcbfghclhalboakcipcmmndhcj
